"MATH_0007": "$B$", "MATH_0008": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0009": "$R$", "MATH_0010": "$k$", "MATH_0011": "$B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-conventions-notation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-orbit-space-locally-finite-type-over-base}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:73993fb96249ad59fd27ec9e883e3d5d8ea9330c29098c7f46631b8950321a67", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:2ca14121a7f443347acd479eb662244ee826ea0732a148668c7c6b72d7a15265", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b4c12f3a320162d30de8b6047c73db0ce100494b0fc3d806223dbe8ad97faed6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> as in Section <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a pre-relation.\nAssume <MATH_0003> are locally of finite type over <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> be an <MATH_0006>-invariant morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0007>.\nThen <MATH_0008> is an orbit space for <MATH_0009> if and only if the natural map\n<MATHSEG_0001>equivalence relation generated by <MATHSEG_0002>\nis bijective for all algebraically closed fields <MATH_0010> over <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ef0ab0c2750bb4a6e5cd1f5e5f85bae6e324da20b162fb746479e08d62735218", "unit_id": "tag:04A0:statement"}
